\section*{Geometric CAT(0) actions for word-hyperbolic groups}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a counterexample in the selected manuscript. A hyperbolic group with a finite classifying complex is claimed to admit no proper and cocompact isometric action with proper complete CAT(0) target.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Result 1.} The source constructs a finite, connected, aspherical simplicial complex \(K\) of dimension two. In its universal cover, a length-\(\ell\) combinatorial loop admits a triangular disk diagram with at most \(C\ell\) faces, for one finite constant \(C\). Nevertheless,
\[
 \pi_1K\text{ has no proper cocompact isometric action on a proper complete CAT}(0)\text{ space}.
\]
The linear filling estimate makes \(\pi_1K\) word-hyperbolic. Within the homotopy class of \(K\), no simplicial complex with finitely many simplices admits a geodesic length metric compatible with its topology and locally CAT(0); the claim also excludes such a locally CAT(-1) metric.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Nested incidence tables produce finite relations with a linear disk-filling bound. Conditional sampling creates a limiting configuration of controlled energy, and its geometric obstruction contradicts any proposed CAT(0) action; the finite aspherical model preserves the topological finiteness claim.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The main theorem gives a word-hyperbolic fundamental group with no proper cocompact action on any proper complete CAT(0) space. This directly violates the target; the extra two-dimensional witness is unnecessary. lean/docs/257.md documents exactly the action obstruction even though it excludes the paper stronger dimension/local-CAT(0) details. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed negative answer to the stated question.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 257, the documented construction gives a finite aspherical hyperbolic group model without a geometric proper-complete CAT(0) action. The stronger dimension-two and all locally CAT(0) model claims are excluded. The listed Comparator files are \texttt{HyperbolicObstruction.lean}. Named declarations include \texttt{OAI.HyperbolicObstruction.main}. This site has not executed the Lean code. The scope descriptions do not certify the remaining manuscript arguments.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these manuscripts to work by an internal model. Its release cautions that arguments without formalization can contain mistakes. This catalogue has not independently checked the proofs; the labels report the mathematical claims attributed to OpenAI.

